# tests/assertions/wordb_vm.rxt — module `assertions`, [M6.2] WAVE B: `\b`/`\B`
# under the VM engine — every block here carries a capturing group, which
# forces VM routing (src/opt/select_engine.c's `forces_captures`) and is what
# gives sabotage S75's `emit_vm.c` arm a corpus population at all (see the
# section comment just below for the measurement that motivated this shard).
#
# ONE OF FOUR SHARDS wordb.rxt was split into 2026-08-21 (see
# wordb_basic.rxt's header for the split rationale and
# tests/assertions/CLAUDE.md for the full list). Every case here moved
# verbatim from wordb.rxt; nothing was added, removed, or reworded.
#
# THE SHARED CONTEXT, restated briefly because it governs every block below
# (full version: wordb_basic.rxt's header). EVERY EXPECTATION WAS PRODUCED BY
# libpcre2 10.46 (through tests/fuzz/pcre2_oracle, options = 0), never
# written by hand, and cross-checked by python3 `re` with 0 divergences.
# `\b`/`\B` are the module's first CONTEXT assertions, so the `ms`/`ns` cells
# below at `startpos > 0` are the VM's own answer to mechanism 4
# (assertions_design.md §3.8) — the VM's guarded spelling (design §9.3) reads
# `s[pos-1]` directly and has no mechanism-4 seed to get wrong, which is why
# these cells are pinned here rather than assumed identical to the DFA's.

# ====================================================================
# THE VM HALF, and it is here because its ABSENCE was
# measured. Every block above is capture-free, so every one
# of them routes to the DFA and NOTHING in this file reached
# src/gen/emit_vm.c's `\b` arm at all -- found by running
# sabotage S75, which points that arm at a different byte set
# and came back with 0 corpus failures out of 3,528.
#
# A capturing group forces the VM (src/opt/select_engine.c's
# `forces_captures`), so these blocks are the same questions
# asked of the other engine -- including the `ms`/`ns` cells,
# since the VM's guarded spelling (design §9.3) reads
# `s[pos-1]` directly and has no mechanism-4 seed to get
# wrong, which is a difference worth having pinned in both
# directions rather than assumed.
# ====================================================================

